From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:01:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] igmp: elect against an older-version querier and query from
 the VLAN's address

Two faults left a snooping VLAN with no router port and the switch querying
as if it were alone, seen on a Celestica DX010 (SONiC 202511) at IGMPv3 on a
LAN whose router queries in IGMPv2:

- igmp_process_query() returned on any version mismatch before the
  querier election and the router-port learning. A v3 snooper (the
  version that takes the IGMPv3 reports Linux hosts send) therefore never
  saw an IGMPv2 querier: rtr_port_list stayed empty, the switch stayed
  querier, and it answered leaves with its own group-specific queries.
  An older-version query is still a querier (RFC 3376 section 7, RFC 4541
  section 2.1.1); only a query newer than the VLAN's version, or one whose
  version cannot be told, is dropped now. Both are still counted.

- ip_get_lowest_ip_address_on_port() and igmp_send_general_query() looked
  for the VLAN's address only through vlan_node->ve_ifindex. SONiC binds
  no VE to a VLAN; l2mcmgrd's INTERFACE_TABLE update stores the address in
  ve_portdb_tree under the VLAN id. This change looks there when
  ve_ifindex is 0, which covers one start-up order only: the next change
  covers the others (ve_ifindex the bare VLAN id, which is what the DX010
  runs with). Queries left from 0.0.0.0 on a VLAN with an address, and an
  address of 0 lost every election.
---
 src/igmp_io.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/igmp_io.c b/src/igmp_io.c
index d38f33e..f9bb14c 100644
--- a/src/igmp_io.c
+++ b/src/igmp_io.c
@@ -251,12 +251,22 @@ void igmp_process_query(MCGRP_CLASS *igmp,
     // Update our operating version if needed
     myver = igmp_vport->oper_version;
 
+    /* A query of an older version than ours is still a querier on the
+     * VLAN (RFC 3376 section 7, RFC 4541 section 2.1.1): elect against it
+     * and learn its port as a router port. Only a query we cannot parse,
+     * or one newer than our version, is dropped. Dropping every
+     * mismatch left a v3 snooper beside an IGMPv2 querier with no router
+     * port and querying as if alone. */
     if (igmpver != igmp_vport->oper_version)
     {
         igmp->igmp_stats[vir_port_id].igmp_wrong_ver_query++;
         igmp_warn_version_mismatch(igmp_pport, igmpver, clnt_src_ip);
-        L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_ERR(vir_port_id, "%s:%d IGMP version mismatch %d !=%d",FN,LN,igmp_vport->oper_version,igmpver);
-        return;
+        if (igmpver == IGMP_VERSION_NONE || igmpver > igmp_vport->oper_version)
+        {
+            L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_ERR(vir_port_id, "%s:%d IGMP version mismatch %d !=%d",FN,LN,igmp_vport->oper_version,igmpver);
+            return;
+        }
+        L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_DEBUG(vir_port_id, "%s:%d IGMPv%d query on a v%d VLAN processed",FN,LN,igmpver,igmp_vport->oper_version);
     }
 
 
@@ -999,6 +1009,12 @@ UINT32 ip_get_lowest_ip_address_on_port(UINT16 port_number, uint8_t type)
         else 
             ip_address = mld_portdb_get_port_lowest_ipv4_addr_from_list(port_number);
     }
+    else if (vlan_node) {
+        /* SONiC binds no VE to the VLAN: l2mcmgrd's INTERFACE_TABLE update
+         * keeps the VLAN interface's addresses in ve_portdb_tree under the
+         * VLAN id itself. */
+        ip_address = ve_mld_portdb_get_port_lowest_ipv4_addr_from_list(gvid);
+    }
     if(ip_address < lowest_ip_address)
         lowest_ip_address = ip_address;
     return (lowest_ip_address);
@@ -1504,6 +1520,12 @@ void igmp_send_general_query( MCGRP_CLASS *igmp,
             L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_DEBUG(tx_port_number, "%s:%d:[vlan:%d] Router ifindex:0x%x port:0x%x ", FN, LN, tx_port_number, vlan_node->ifindex,port_id);
         }
     }
+    else if (vlan_node) {
+        /* No VE on SONiC: the VLAN interface's addresses, by VLAN id (see
+         * ip_get_lowest_ip_address_on_port). Without this every general
+         * query left from 0.0.0.0. */
+        sptr_addr_entry = (port_link_list_t *)(portdb_get_port_lowest_ipv4_addr_from_list(ve_mld_portdb_tree, gvid));
+    }
 
 
     L2MCD_VLAN_LOG_DEBUG(tx_port_number, "%s:%d:[vlan:%d] phy_port:0x%x version:%d vlan:%d ", 
